{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/941614-what-s-your-favorite-non-core-hunter-groups","id":941614,"title":"What's your favorite non-core Hunter groups?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-01T19:29:17-07:00","id":941614,"title":"What's your favorite non-core Hunter groups?","content":"I can't help but notice that Hunter discussions over the years barely ever seem to touch on the Compacts and Conspiracies introduced in later supplememts, and it's always struck me as criminal. I'm definitely hoping some of them can sneak into the new edition of the game, but in the meantime I figured we should have a thread about them. <br /> <br /> I've been a longtime fan of Division Six, as they're basically Delta Green with even less support and the serial numbers filed off; the idea of a bunch of unarmed, untrained schmucks who think they're the lone government conspiracy standing against the untangling of the universe itself. They often get painted as dupes (their official art with the chubby awful guy really doesn't help), but I love the idea of playing them straight as a gritty group of scared men and women. They also make stellar antagonists; the mental image of a black van full of Sleepers smashing through the wall of your player's Sanctum and unloading uzis is worth the cost of the entire book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:32:18-07:00","id":941645,"title":"","content":"Among conspiracies it's easily the Knights of St. George. For all your philanthropic millionaire with a secret life as Conan-like sorcerer slayer needs. Solid group, great motivation and history, powers could use some work but definitely gets the feel of the whole 'mystery cult' vibe first edition struggled for in some places.<br /> <br /> For compacts I also liked Division Six but my favorite would probably be the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood. Very easy to put into play, and like Division Six has a wide variety of 'types' you can have in it, plus they're the kind of group that can be introduced as and even act as a normal organization until they get provoked.<br /> <br /> A couple heartbreakers would probably be VASCU, who fall short to me by not really seeming to go anywhere. A nice idea, they have the job, the authority, the federal government behind them, you can really tap into the blue books for it, they're psychic profilers and it stops there. It seems like there should have been more to it. And among the compacts the Promethean Brotherhood. Great compact, great motivation, trammeled by the mechanics of the Rite of Hecate which takes great risk and effort to perform for very meager, and more importantly temporary, gains. This seems to be a weird aspect of first edition where some powers were curbed from being too powerful. The Faithful of Shulpae, a runner up for favorites, does what they do so much better. I have to imagine the Faithful would convert Prometheans within minutes of explaining what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:42:06-07:00","id":941651,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> I think the best part of VASCU has nothing to do with serial killers or psychic powers; they're the only Hunters who have to go build a case and arrest the monsters instead of just trying to murder them. That alone makes them more distinct and interesting than nearly every other Conspiracy, because of how novel that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T21:10:34-07:00","id":941666,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Bear Lodge and Barrett Commission are my top picks, Talbot Group and Night Watch come in at a close second. I'd definitely love to see things expanded on, like what's so valuable in that lost hunting lodge or how the commission deals with conspiracies that would try to take them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T00:16:09-07:00","id":941738,"title":"","content":"among the conspiracies, my vote is for the Knights of St George. Their Templar like atmosphere, the theme of lies upon lies upon lies and their connection to goetic magic and symbolism are simply too cool to ignore, IMO. I had tons of fun with them, and creating a lot of different origin stories for what the Faceless Angels actually are (eventually I use them as abyssal Annunaki for most cases, but still the thought experiments were fun). In sort, I find them really interesting and compelling to play.<br /> <br /> As for a compact, I have two- the first is also from Witch Finders: the Keepers of the Source. Their ability to locate Hallows and similar mystical sites and works toward protecting the &quot;Mother Earth&quot; just draws me, even if it is terribly misguided (in my games it is not that misguided, but oh well). While they were my top favorite for a long, long time, since Dark Eras the Scarlet Watch stole their place- their duty to their family and big focus around blood bonds and loyalty beyond space and time is just awesome to me, with them being bound by blood and fate to carry their ancient mission and fight blood sucking demons- and this is from a guy who usually like bastards and backstabbers (the Ashwood Abbey are my favorite compact at all, and the Promethean Brotherhood comes after the Watch and the Keepers). Plus, their all &quot;fallen conspiracy&quot; atmosphere and the potential at reconstructing their former power and influence gives a lot new plot hooks, and the blood oath which binds them together (which also gives me a bit of a lovecraftian feeling in how it was described) is also a great plot hook.<br /> <br /> As you may guess from those two favorites, yes, it means I'm just waiting for the opportunity to play at a Doubting Souls setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T02:09:18-07:00","id":941774,"title":"","content":"I like Les Mysteres, albeit I prefer to center their cosmology solely in voodoo rather than trying to make them pseudo dreamspeakers. <br /> Still trying to modify Rites Du Cheval in a sort of mini magic system centered in loa possesion, without the usual endowment point progression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 08-02-2016, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T20:35:03-07:00","id":942448,"title":"","content":"The Knights of Saint Adrian are a bit goofy, but I've always played GMC and DtD with a fair amount of absurdity mixed in with the horror (secret passages under Disney World, killer animatronics, Foodfight! has occult secrets hidden in the backgrounds of some of the shots, etc), so they don't really clash that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T21:44:12-07:00","id":942481,"title":"","content":"If I had to choose, my two favorite non-core Compacts would probably be Divison Six and Utopia Now. The former I love because of the way they flip the concept of the top secret license-to-kill power fantasy on its head (amusing considering one can play said fantasy completely straight with TFV and a lesser extent VASCU). The latter I love because it reminds me of the weird conspiracy theories I used to read online as a kid. There's something oddly nostalgic and wistful about the mash up of vaguely Randian philosophy with paranoid Tom Clancy techno-thriller, at least to me. I also enjoy thinking about them as archaeologists of a parallel present, mining miraculous technologies out of the broken and abandoned timelines left behind by the God Machine.<br /> <br /> My two favorite non-core Conspiracies are VASCU and the Knights of St Adrian. VASCU occupies a weird space, simultaneously sharing too much of its general schtick with TFV while also being too narrowly focused on Slashers. They work for me though, and I have typically house ruled away the two main issues I have with them. The Knights I love because tattoo magic is literally always a good place to start, all the moreso because it doubles as a sort of weird technology that itself generates tons of thematic potential and plot hooks. I even dig that this &quot;Knightly Order&quot; are really a group of skip-tracers that stumbled a little too deep into the world of the God Machine. Even the persona of Saint Adrian, if its an angle you want to play up, can be entertaining as the patron saint of mercenaries and arms dealers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T05:25:02-07:00","id":942649,"title":"","content":"Knights of Saint George was love at first sight.<br /> <br /> I always liked the compact in one of the Vampire Night Horrors books, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T14:37:08-07:00","id":943005,"title":"","content":"Ahl al-Jabal, becuase it pretty much nails its portrayal of a hunter group comprised of Nizari Ismaili Muslims as square on the head as you possibly can in terms of accuracy and appropriate portrayal. It is so good that you could use it to educate someone about the actual basics of Ismaili faith, minus the vampire hunting and dual-weapon wielding. <br /> <br /> Although it's very new, Keepers of the Word is another that I really like. Then again, I am highly biased in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:22:22-07:00","id":958159,"title":"","content":"I always has a soft sport for the Bear Lodge, they had a really simple outlook; but you can take in interesting directions when they interact with the wider world of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:26:00-07:00","id":958186,"title":"","content":"Ami San.<br /> <br /> Though quite hampered by word count (their subgroups especially; the Sea Whistle needed to be an Endowment and they needed an actual Endowment). But I really like how they're basically powered by having a healthy community. It makes a strong contrast to how isolated most hunters are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}